# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# EXP-1: the fog covers the squares the party has not been near, and
# nothing else on the screen (M5-E5f #263, M5-E5g #299).
# A pair leg, and it can be one: this seam claims no key, being a setting
# rather than a command (`seam_explored.cpp`), so every keystroke reaches
# the program in both halves and the two runs differ by the flag alone.
# A covered square is half covered: a one-pixel checkerboard of palette
# index 0, black, with the program's own pixel on the other half. The
# reveal radius is zero, so the trail is one square wide.
# Not driven since #299; the rects and phase boundaries below are derived
# from the geometry and the key cadence, and #293 owes it a re-drive.

about the fog covers the squares the party has not been near, and nothing else
kind pair
program START.EXE
both code-wheel

# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), pinned by
# digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam explored
until 260000000
every 25

# A screen may appear in the two runs a dump apart, because a repaint
# lands where it lands. One dump of slack, measured (#234).
slack 1

# Slot J: the one shipped save whose party is already standing on a
# wilderness area (docs/explored-overlay.md §4). Eight steps north, 150
# frames apart, which is the cadence every driven walk in this tree uses.
key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key J@9201
key Up@10600
key Up@10750
key Up@10900
key Up@11050
key Up@11200
key Up@11350
key Up@11500
key Up@11650

# The window is 120 by 120 at (8, 8) and a square is 24 by 24, so these are
# whole squares of it, and they are the fogged squares rather than a box
# round them. The party is the window's middle column throughout: the two
# columns each side of it are fog for their whole height, `ahead` is its
# own column above it, `behind` its own column below it, and `tail` the
# lower half of `behind`, which stays fog for one step longer.
rect ahead 56,8,79,55
rect west 8,8,55,127
rect east 80,8,127,127
rect behind 56,80,79,127
rect tail 56,104,79,127

# The whole run up to the arrival: not one pixel. The mode byte becomes 3
# at frame 9,552 and the screen settles at 10,275, where the fog appears.
allow 0-10250 none

# Arrived, with one square stood on: everything but that square.
allow 10275-10650 ahead west east behind

# One step north (the key at 10,600, allowed the same 75 frames to land as
# every other phase boundary here): the square the party came from is
# window row 3 and is clear, and row 4 is still fog.
allow 10675-10800 ahead west east tail

# From the second step on, the two squares below the party are both squares
# it has stood on, and the trail is one column wide.
allow 10825-end ahead west east
